<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand I of Austria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1793–1875</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> was emperor from 1835 to 1848, also king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/illyria">Illyria</a>. Suffering from epilepsy, he left government to a regency council dominated by Metternich. During the revolutions of 1848 he was persuaded to abdicate in favour of his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-joseph-i">Franz Joseph I</a>, and he lived quietly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague">Prague</a> until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-austria.jpg" alt="Ferdinand I of Austria" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Eduard Edlinger · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaiser_Ferdinand_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
